  The campaign also produced a claimed _natural-density_ upgrade of Tao's theorem @tao2022: the set ${N : "Col"_min (N) > N_0}$ would have upper natural density at most $C log^(-1\/25) N_0$, hence $"Col"_min (N) <= f(N)$ for almost all $N$ in natural density, for every $f arrow.r infinity$. The claimed proof includes a proof of the object of Tao's Remark 1.16 (fine-scale mixing of the entire affine map $(S_n, X_n)$), which Tao described as "plausibly attainable from the methods in this paper." The manuscript (`notes/round4-july2026/s5-completion/PROOFS.md`, 571 lines) was produced by an AI agent and adversarially reviewed by two independent AI referees, neither of which refuted it (minor findings; every Tao citation verified against the arXiv v7 text; all verification scripts pass). *It has not been reviewed by a human expert, and it is not part of this paper's claims.* It should be treated exactly as an unrefereed preprint draft: a candidate theorem awaiting review by a human analytic number theorist, nothing more. The vetted claim boundary of the repository (`proof-obligations.md`) is unchanged by it.
